<title>HONG KONG: VTech interim net rises 30.1 percent.</title>
<headline>VTech interim net rises 30.1 percent.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ended September 30</p>
<p>(in million US$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (U.S. cents)	   16.8  vs 13.2</p>
<p>    Dividend (U.S. cents)    3.0   vs 2.5</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  nil   vs 0.6 loss</p>
<p>    Net			    26.8  vs 20.6</p>
<p>    Turnover		     355.2 vs 365.1</p>
<p>    Company name		 VTech Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  December 25-29, 1996</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   January 9, 1997</p>
<p>NOTE - VTech is a consumer electronics manufacturer.</p>
<p>At the annual general meeting held on September 11, 1996, the company approved a bonus issue of one share of US$0.05 each of the company for every five ordinary shares held at October 3, 1996. Share earnings for the period after adjustment for the bonus issue in October, would be 14 U.S. cents against 11 U.S. cents for 1995.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
